---
// src/pages/terms.astro

import '../styles/global.css'
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Terms of Use — PayMeDash</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Terms of use for the PayMeDash point-of-sale software." />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
</head>
<body class="min-h-dvh bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 via-blue-50 to-indigo-100 dark:from-slate-900 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-indigo-950 text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 flex flex-col gap-8">

        <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
            <a href="/" class="text-sm text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">&larr; PayMeDash</a>
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Terms of Use</h1>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                These terms cover the PayMeDash point-of-sale software and the PayMeDash API. By
                taking a payment with PayMeDash, or by paying through a terminal that runs it, you
                accept them. If you do not accept them, do not use the software.
            </p>
        </header>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. What PayMeDash is</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                PayMeDash is open-source software that a merchant runs to accept cryptocurrency
                payments and receive DASH. It is not a bank, a money transmitter, an exchange, a
                broker, or a custodian. It does not hold your funds at any point, and it cannot
                reverse, freeze, or recover a payment once it has settled.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. The merchant is the seller</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                The sale is between you and the merchant operating the terminal. The merchant sets the
                prices, the DASH payout address that receives the funds, and any refund policy. The
                PayMeDash project is not a party to the sale and is not responsible for the goods,
                services, or conduct of any merchant.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Conversion is performed by 1Click</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                When you pay in a cryptocurrency other than DASH, the conversion into DASH is carried
                out by <strong>1Click</strong>, a third-party swap service operated at
                <code class="font-mono text-xs">1click.chaindefuser.com</code>. PayMeDash submits the
                request to it but does not operate it and does not control it. Rates, availability, and
                the minimum amount accepted are set by that service, and its own terms apply to the
                swap itself.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Amounts, rates, and minimums</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                The DASH amount you must send is calculated from a rate at the moment it is quoted. A
                rate is not a promise: cryptocurrency prices move, and a quote is valid only for the
                short period stated with it. A sale below the minimum accepted by the swap service
                cannot proceed; the minimum is shown before you pay. If you send less than the stated
                amount, the payment may fail, be delayed, or be refunded rather than completed, and
                network fees may be deducted from any refund.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Refunds</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                A swap that cannot be completed is refunded by the swap service to the refund target
                recorded with the request. Unless you supply an address on your own chain, the refund
                is issued to a NEAR Intents account held by the operator, from which it must be
                withdrawn. Refunds are not instant and are not guaranteed against a loss in value
                between payment and refund.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Your responsibilities</h2>
            <ul class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-1">
                <li>Send only the asset shown, using the deposit address and amount shown for that payment.</li>
                <li>Verify the destination address shown matches what you intend before sending.</li>
                <li>Do not use the software where doing so would break the law that applies to you.</li>
                <li>Keep your own wallet credentials safe. PayMeDash never has access to them.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. No warranty</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, whether express or
                implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
                particular purpose, and non-infringement. It depends on third-party networks and
                services that may be slow, unavailable, or faulty. You use it at your own risk.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                To the fullest extent permitted by law, the authors and contributors of PayMeDash are
                not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary
                damages, including loss of funds, loss of profit, or loss of data, arising from the use
                of or inability to use the software, or from any transaction made through it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">9. Changes</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
                These terms may change as the software changes. The version in effect is the one
                published on this page at the time you use the software.
            </p>
        </section>

        <footer class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
            <p>See also the <a href="/privacy" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Privacy</a> page.</p>
        </footer>

    </main>
</body>
</html>